<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> White-based hatebear architectures
    apply rigorous, dual-axis tactical pressure: deploying relentless
    early clocks via protected threats (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Mother of Runes">Mother of Runes</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Silver Knight">Silver Knight</a
    >) while simultaneously attacking operational mana
    development through terminal <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Armageddon">Armageddon</a
    > resolutions. Prioritize fetchland activations for basic lands
    early, and conserve instant-speed interaction (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >) exclusively for high-leverage combat clocks or protective
    enablers.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Trim sensitive mana investments
    and slow selection engines. Bring in <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > to dominate the board as an untargetable morph presence prior
    to land wipes, alongside <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    > and defensive spot interaction. Establishing physical combat
    equilibrium before an Armageddon hits the stack completely defuses
    their strategic win condition.
</p>
